### (3_1)  Basic Idea of Mutual Exclusion ###

mutual exclusion - a way of making sure that if one process is executing the CS, then other process cannot enter the CS
                   until the executing process comes out of the CS.

1) mutual exclusion
2) progress
3) bounded waiting


### (3_2)  Basic Idea of Mprogress ###

progress - a way of making sure that if a process is not inside the CS(ir it is in NCS), then it will not block other process from entering the CS.

### (3_3)  Basic Idea of bounded waiting ###

bounded waiting - a way of making sure that there wxists a bound (or limit) on the number of times other processes are allowed to enter the CS after a process has made a request to enter the CS and before that request is granted.

